# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# Local SQLite (backend projector dev DB, created on `cargo run -p kanade-backend`).
# Production deploys store this under /var/lib/kanade or C:\ProgramData\Kanade.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Release-staging output from scripts\build-release.ps1
# (kanade-<role>.exe + <role>.toml + deploy-<role>.ps1 per role,
# optionally a sibling .zip when -Zip is passed).
/dist/

# NOTE: kata-managed base block (begin/end markers below) sits just
# after this point. The Rust ignores above live OUTSIDE the kata
# section so they're owned by the project, not the pj-base template.
# pj-rust ships a similar Rust-block as its own layer once that seed
# is wired up — at which point the manual entries above can be removed
# and re-introduced via `kata apply`.

# kata:gitignore:base:begin
# Editor / OS noise — kata-managed (yukimemi/pj-base).
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# APM dependencies — install output of apm.yml's deps.
# Skill files under .agents/, .claude/, .gemini/ etc. are
# committed (kata seeds them; renri post_create refreshes via
# `apm install --update`); the apm_modules/ source cache is not.
apm_modules/
# kata:gitignore:base:end
